 ## Overview
-Scatter Samples to Image is a post-processing step that scatters computed sample values from arbitrary screen-space positions into a regular image grid [S1, unofficial]. It maps non-uniformly distributed samples to a standard raster image for visualization. Unlike [Splatting](23-splatting.md), which uses geometric kernels to blur and accumulate contributions, this method performs a direct assignment of values to pixel coordinates without filtering [S1, unofficial].
